[exl3-serve] WP16 prefix checkpoints ON: 59.8 MB per checkpoint (GDN S 56.6 MB + conv 2.9 MB over 36 GDN layers, PLE ring 0.18 MB, head-fill carry 0.041 MB, + the host PLE n-gram pair); cap 4 GiB (--prefix-ckpt-mem-gb; default 4 is a placeholder — the owner sets the final default) = 71 checkpoint(s) = 3.95 GiB at most, allocated lazily, LRU across slots, kept across a conversation's cache-hit turns. Taken at chunk ends of aligned prefills (grid from 0 or from an aligned checkpoint; never after a prompt-end prefix hit): end % 8192 == 0, plus every C=4095 boundary in a prefill's last 2 chunks; keyed by C. Resumed on a prompt-end miss from the deepest checkpoint <= min(LCP, plen-1) (a 128K document holds ~18 = ~1.0 GiB)
[exl3-serve] C1 tail checkpoints ON (prefix.tail_ckpt = 1 / --prefix-tail-ckpt=1|2: only splits absorbed into an existing chunk boundary; OUTPUT-CHANGING, owner consent): every prefill also checkpoints at its message boundary (the prompt without its generation prompt) minus 8 tokens when that saves >= 128 tokens over the C grid point below it; runs are realigned to the C grid; the next chat turn resumes there
