[req] tool_call  call_16 write({"path":"/Users/sean/repo.opensource/VeloBench/AGENTS.md","content":"# AGENTS.md\n\nVeloBenchmark (`velobench`) — a single-binary LLM benchmarking / live-stats console.\nRust (Axum) backend that embeds and serves an Angular frontend via `include_dir!`.\nAGPL-3.0. See `README.md` for product scope; `docs/` for user-facing detail.\n\n## Build & run (order matters)\n\nThe frontend is compiled into the binary at `cargo build` time, so the frontend\n**must** be built first whenever it changed:\n\n```bash\nnpm --prefix frontend install          # first time only\nbash scripts/build-frontend.sh         # Angular build -> assets/ (embedded)\ncargo build --release                  # -> target/release/velobench\n./target/release/velobench --host 0.0.0.0 --port 13843\n```\n\n- **`protoc` (≥3.x) is a hard build prerequisite.** `build.rs` shells out to\n  `prost-build` to compile `proto/velobench.proto`. Missing `protoc` = failed build.\n- Node ≥ 20 required for the frontend.\n- Dev loop: `cd frontend && npm start` (Angular live-reload on :4200, proxy API/WS to\n  the backend) alongside `cargo run --release`.\n\n## Wire protocol\n\n- `proto/velobench.proto` is the **single source of truth** for the streaming wire\n  protocol. Rust side regenerates via `build.rs`/`prost` on `cargo build`; browser\n  side regenerates via `pbjs`/`pbts` inside `scripts/build-frontend.sh` (writes\n  `frontend/src/app/proto/velobench.{js,d.ts}`). Edit the `.proto`, not the generated files.\n\n## Embedded assets\n\n- Everything under `assets/` is embedded into the binary, including\n  `assets/test_images/` (the vision-test image library). **Adding/replacing an image\n  or any embedded asset requires a frontend build + `cargo build` to take effect.**\n- `scripts/build-frontend.sh` wipes stale hashed bundles in `assets/` and preserves a\n  user-provided `assets/favicon.ico` and `assets/payloads/`. Don't commit generated\n  `assets/*.js`/`*.css` — they're gitignored and regenerated.\n\n## Backend architecture\n\n- `src/main.rs` = entrypoint (clap CLI: `--host`/`--port`/`--data-dir`, defaults\n  `0.0.0.0`/`13843`/`velobench_data`). All Axum routes are registered in\n  `src/server.rs`; each feature is its own top-level module under `src/`\n  (chat proxy in `proxy.rs`, concurrency in `concurrent.rs`, classification in\n  `classify.rs`, telemetry/OTLP receiver in `telemetry.rs`, stats in `stats.rs`,\n  tokenizer in `tokenizer.rs`, persistence in `state.rs`).\n- **Axum 0.8 path syntax is `{param}`, not `:param`** (e.g. `/api/tests/{id}`). Match\n  the existing routes when adding endpoints.\n- Live streaming also flows over one WebSocket (`/ws`, `src/ws.rs`); telemetry uses its\n  own WS (`/api/telemetry/ws`).\n\n## Runtime / data\n\n- On first boot the server creates `velobench_data/` in the **current working\n  directory** (settings, sessions, tests, comparisons). Run from where you want data to\n  live, or pass `--data-dir`.\n- API keys are stored **server-side** in `velobench_data/settings.json`, never in the\n  browser. There is **no auth** — intended for trusted networks.\n- Built-in tests are re-seeded on every start; user tests/favourites/sessions persist.\n\n## Tests & verification\n\n- Rust: `cargo test` (unit tests gated by `#[cfg(test)]`, e.g. `src/corpus_test.rs`).\n  `cargo clippy` / `cargo fmt` for lint/format. Release profile uses LTO + single\n  codegen unit (slower builds, expected).\n- Frontend: `ng test` (Karma/Jasmine) run from `frontend/`. No e2e configured.\n\n## Releasing\n\n- Tag-push (`git tag v0.1.0 && git push --tags`) triggers `.github/workflows/release.yml`,\n  which builds all four platform tarballs and attaches them to the release. Artifacts\n  must be named exactly `velobenchmark-<os>-<arch>.tar.gz` — that's what `install.sh`\n  downloads. See `docs/building.md` / `RELEASING.md`."})
