[req] raw model output (997 chars): "Found it. Here's the relevant section of `/documents/config.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\n# Database Configuration\ndb:\n  host: localhsot\n  port: 5432\n  name: myapp_prod\n  pool_size: 10\n```\n\n**The typo:** On line 3, the database host value is `localhsot` — the characters `o` and `s` are transposed. It's a misspelling of `localhost`.\n\n**The fix:** Change line 3 from:\n\n```yaml\n  host: localhsot\n```\n\nto:\n\n```yaml\n  host: localhost\n```\n\n**Why it matters:** `localhsot` isn't a resolvable hostname, so any DNS lookup will fail and the application will be unable to connect to the database (typically surfacing as a \"name or service not known\" / connection-refused error) even though Postgres is running locally on port `5432`.\n\n**One caveat:** this file is currently mounted with `read` permissions only (`write: false`), so the edit can't be applied in place through my file tools. You'll need to either update it in your source control/editor, or remount it with write access and I can apply the change for you."
