[req] raw model output (3128 chars): "Here's a ready-to-paste prompt for OpenCode. It's grounded in the actual code surface (`HelperConfig` in `src/settings.rs`, the OpenAI-compatible call sites in `src/classify.rs` and `src/analyze.rs`) so the investigating agent doesn't wander.\n\n---\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> Investigate replacing VeloBench's **Helper Model** configuration with **CLM** (Contrastive Language Models, https://github.com/Contrastive-LM/CLM). This is a research/spike task — produce findings and a proposed design, don't commit implementation yet.\n>\n> **Context (already in this repo):**\n> - The Helper Model is defined as `HelperConfig` in `src/settings.rs` (base_url + key + model id + concurrency) and is exposed in the Settings UI (\"Helper Model\" tab, currently `qwen3.8-flash-next` on provider `gb10`).\n> - It is consumed as an **OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint** in exactly two places: `src/classify.rs` (`resolve_helper` + the classification request, expects the model to return a dominant regime + ordered regime list as JSON) and `src/analyze.rs` (post-hoc session meta-analysis). Read both before proposing anything.\n> - VeloBench is a single Rust binary that embeds the Angular frontend; `AGENTS.md` document"
